course: dictionary
lesson: 14623
title: The portrayal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A portrayal is the way someone or something is shown or described. It can be in a picture, a film, a play, a book or a news story. «The film gave a funny portrayal of a teacher» means the film showed a teacher as funny.
explain: An actor's portrayal is the way they play a character. «Sam's portrayal of the king was so strong that the whole class clapped» means Sam played the king in a way that impressed everyone.
explain: Good readers judge a portrayal. Is it fair, true, kind or one-sided? «The book's portrayal of the village made it seem dull and grey, but the village is lovely» is an unfair portrayal, because it leaves out the good things. Ask yourself: does this picture match real life?
fact: A portrayal is a way of showing or describing someone or something.
fact: «A realistic portrayal» means it shows things as they really are.
fact: «An unfair portrayal» means it shows something in a one-sided or untrue way.
fact: An actor's portrayal is the way they play a character on stage or on screen.
fact: To judge a portrayal, ask: is it fair, true, kind, or does it leave out important parts?
exercise: «The museum gave a realistic portrayal of life in Roman times.» What does portrayal mean here? | The price of a meal | A ticket to get into the museum | A painting that was stolen | *The way Roman life was shown
exercise: «His portrayal of the king made everyone laugh.» What is his portrayal? | A long journey by ship | *The way he played the king | A kind of tea | A gold crown worn for a party
exercise: Which phrase means a picture that is fair and true to life? | a loud portrayal | *a realistic portrayal | an unfair portrayal
test: «The film's portrayal of the hero was one-sided: he was always right and everyone else was wrong.» Is this portrayal fair? | *No, it is one-sided | It is a painting of a hero | Yes, it is perfectly fair and balanced
test: «Kira's portrayal of Mary Poppins was loved by the audience.» What is a portrayal, here? | *The way a character is shown or played | The lights on the stage | A written ticket for the show | A list of all the actors in the play
exam: In one sentence, what makes a portrayal unfair? | It uses too many pictures | It is written in capital letters | It is always too long | *It shows something in a one-sided or untrue way
